{
  "$comment": "When a window refills, in the words every Quota client uses. Relative is the default: a countdown under a day, then a local weekday and 24-hour time, then a month and day. Absolute always uses the local date. English is fixed; weekday and month cases pin `now` and `resets_at` as RFC 3339 with an offset so every runtime formats that local time. `packages/quota-model`, `packages/apple-shared` FreshnessCopy, `apps/web/src/lib/format.ts`, and `packages/service` `copy.rs` all answer this file.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "the last second before a minute still rounds up to a minute",
      "seconds_until": 59,
      "now": "2026-09-07T14:00:00-07:00",
      "resets_at": "2026-09-07T14:00:59-07:00",
      "relative": "Resets in 1m",
      "absolute": "Resets Mon 14:00"
    },
    {
      "name": "a whole minute is the first exact minute",
      "seconds_until": 60,
      "now": "2026-09-07T14:00:00-07:00",
      "resets_at": "2026-09-07T14:01:00-07:00",
      "relative": "Resets in 1m",
      "absolute": "Resets Mon 14:01"
    },
    {
      "name": "the last second before an hour rounds up into the hour",
      "seconds_until": 3599,
      "now": "2026-09-07T14:00:00-07:00",
      "resets_at": "2026-09-07T14:59:59-07:00",
      "relative": "Resets in 1h",
      "absolute": "Resets Mon 14:59"
    },
    {
      "name": "an hour drops the zero minutes",
      "seconds_until": 3600,
      "now": "2026-09-07T14:00:00-07:00",
      "resets_at": "2026-09-07T15:00:00-07:00",
      "relative": "Resets in 1h",
      "absolute": "Resets Mon 15:00"
    },
    {
      "name": "three hours exactly omits the minutes",
